{
 "manufacturer": "Swegon",
 "manufacturer_slug": "swegon",
 "model": "CONDUCTOR W4 room controller (airflow and water, Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "conductor-w4",
 "short_model": "CONDUCTOR W4",
 "aliases": [
  "CONDUCTOR RE W4",
  "CONDUCTOR RE W4 1",
  "Conductor W4"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Thermostat / room controller (chilled beam with measured airflow and CO2)",
 "applies_to": "Swegon CONDUCTOR W4 room controller, software 1.12 (technical manual updated 2014-11-21).",
 "summary": "CONDUCTOR W4 is the Swegon room controller for rooms with measured supply and extract airflow plus waterborne cooling and heating, with optional CO2 control. This map covers its alarms, sensor temperatures, damper and valve outputs, airflow level settings in l/s, CO2 control limits, PI tuning and a 39xx commissioning block. Temperature setpoints and the measured airflow, pressure and CO2 readings are left out because the manual gives no scaling for them.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "Tables print 0x/1x/3x/4x reference numbers; subtract 1 for the wire address in each table (4x3921 = holding register 3920)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": "1.12",
 "source": {
  "title": "CONDUCTOR W4 Technical Manual",
  "doc_number": "cond_w4-sw112-m (SW version 1.12)",
  "revision_date": "2014-11-21",
  "url": "https://www.swegon.com/siteassets/_products-documents-archive/waterborne-climate-systems/control-equipment/_en/cond_w4-sw112-m.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 63-69 (Modbus register)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Addresses are printed in Modicon form (0x coils, 1x discrete inputs, 3x input registers, 4x holding registers); wire address = number - 1 within each table.",
  "Sensor temperatures and battery voltage carry an explicit 1:10 scaling. Room temperature (3x0060), changeover temperature (3x0061) and the room-unit setpoint/flow readings (3x0031/3x0032) give a unit but no scaling, so they are left out.",
  "Left out: every temperature setpoint in the holding table (4x0021-4x0030, including the two 'TC/TH Not used' rows, and manual temperature 4x0063). The table gives °C ranges but no scaling, while the input temperatures are marked 1:10, so the raw format is not settled.",
  "Also left out: the 16-register component name (ASCII byte order not given), application ID, serial number, software version and boot-year registers (no format given), and every Not used row.",
  "BMS port settings are menu parameters P_101 (address 1-247), P_102 (baud 9.6/19.2/38.4 k), P_103 (parity odd/even/none) and P_104 (stop bits).",
  "Left out: 4x3911 commissioning command (packs air and water states into the two bytes; the value list is cut off in the manual).",
  "Also left out: the measured airflows (3x0057-3x0059), duct pressures (3x0034-3x0036) and room CO2 (3x0062), which carry only a unit (l/s, Pa, ppm) with no range or scaling; PID outputs 3x0049-3x0052 (signed -100 to 100 % range, signed format never stated); and the commissioning read-backs 4x3921-4x3924 and 4x3940, which give no unit or format."
 ],
